    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s action, **Cal Raleigh** stands as our premier offensive anchor. With a score of 61.37, he earns the start behind the plate against Baz, benefiting significantly from his elevated spot in the order (#2). While the platoon disadvantage against a right-handed arm drags his efficiency slightly, his raw power profile remains our most reliable asset in the absence of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Daulton Varsho**, who all remain sidelined on the IL. We are looking for **Cal Raleigh** to capitalize on a favorable park factor, even as we navigate a roster thinned by injury.\n\nThe bench decision process was most difficult regarding the utility slot, where **Taylor Ward** just barely edges out other options with a 43.69 efficiency score. While he faces a stiff test against Woo, his lead-off position (#1) provides enough volume to justify the start over speculative plays. Conversely, **Bryson Stott** sits at a 41.43 score; he is essentially a coin-flip start today, hampered by an unfavorable matchup against Manaea. His efficiency is being buoyed by favorable wind conditions blowing out, but he remains the first candidate to be subbed out if our cap management requires a more conservative approach tonight. **Masyn Winn** and **Lawrence Butler** round out the active core, with **Masyn Winn** offering a stable 50.24 floor and **Lawrence Butler** providing high-upside potential in a hitters' park, provided his projected #7 spot in the lineup holds firm once the official card is posted. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding **Lawrence Butler** and his \"Lineup Pending\" status; should he drop out of the order entirely or slide into a less advantageous spot, we may need to rotate in depth pieces like **Tyler Freeman**, **Yainer Diaz**, or **Jonathan Aranda**. Additionally, the scarcity of stolen bases remains our primary tactical concern. Since none of our starters today possess the elite sprint speed to move the needle in that category, we are forced to rely on the cumulative output of **Matt Chapman**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, and **Dylan Beavers** in future rotations to keep pace in the SB category. With **Gleyber Torres**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Drew Gilbert** all currently observing bench roles or off-days, our margin for error remains thin\u2014monitor the weather reports for any late-breaking wind shifts that could further suppress the scoring potential of **Bryson Stott**.",
